Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: allocate QMI AFC memory region (type 0xA)

QCN9274 WLAN.WBE.1.6 firmware requests a target memory segment of type
0xA (AFC_REGION_TYPE in the QCA downstream driver).  ath12k does not know
this type and hands the firmware a NULL chunk for it.  This is carried
for the intermittent WMI init failures seen on SBE1V1K WSI radios.

Name the region type and allocate it like the other plain DMA regions.

[SBE1V1K: re-created from https://github.com/OneNAS-space/Askey_Spectrum_SBE1V1K/blob/b6fc7b1f43e7cd6b37373bda8442cb183992e55b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath12k/701-wifi-ath12k-support-memory-type-10.patch
 / https://github.com/Jackie264/SBE1V1K/blob/b8bbbe7cc9c8140a8dd53fd1a9d410bc8195bd0c/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath12k/701-ath12k-support-memory-type-10.patch (author: Jackie <jackie.han@gmail.com>),
 which used a bare "case 10:" (and space indentation in the Jackie264/SBE1V1K copy).
 Ref: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/issues/24949]
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
@@ -2651,6 +2651,7 @@ static int ath12k_qmi_alloc_target_mem_chunk(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 		case PAGEABLE_MEM_REGION_TYPE:
 		case CALDB_MEM_REGION_TYPE:
 		case LPASS_SHARED_V01_REGION_TYPE:
+		case AFC_REGION_TYPE:
 			ret = ath12k_qmi_alloc_chunk(ab, chunk);
 			if (ret)
 				goto err;
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.h
@@ -178,6 +178,7 @@ enum ath12k_qmi_target_mem {
 	CALDB_MEM_REGION_TYPE = 0x4,
 	MLO_GLOBAL_MEM_REGION_TYPE = 0x8,
 	PAGEABLE_MEM_REGION_TYPE = 0x9,
+	AFC_REGION_TYPE = 0xa,
 	LPASS_SHARED_V01_REGION_TYPE = 0xb,
 };
 
